# Data — reproducible from notebooks/scripts, never commit.
# Anchored so the Python subpackage `src/foodsafety/data/` (which contains
# `labels.py`) is NOT silently ignored by an unanchored `data/` pattern.
/data/
# Web-app data JSONs: the two cross-team contract artifacts (scores.json,
# inspection_history.json) are tracked so deployments work without a separate
# data-sync step. Everything else under app/public/data/ is gitignored except
# the small demo fallback (scores_mock.json) that loadScores() falls back to
# when scores.json is absent on a fresh clone.
# Note: a leaf-level pattern is required here. Git's negation rule does NOT
# re-include files whose parent directory is excluded, so we can't write
# `/app/public/data/` + `!scores_mock.json`.
/app/public/data/*.json
!/app/public/data/scores_mock.json
!/app/public/data/scores.json
!/app/public/data/inspection_history.json
!/app/public/data/methodology.json
**/_partial_*/

